# Append-only data files: keep both sides of a conflict instead of failing.
#
# The collector appends a row per race every hour from GitHub Actions, and
# local runs append too. Git's default merge sees two sets of lines added at
# the end of the same file and calls it a conflict, so every pull after a
# local collection needed manual resolution, and the usual fix of taking one
# side silently discarded the other's rows.
#
# union keeps both sets. For a file where every line is an independent
# observation and order carries no meaning, that is exactly right: two
# collectors appending different rows should produce a file with all of
# them.
#
# It would be wrong for anything where lines depend on each other, which is
# why this is scoped to these files rather than to data/ as a whole.
data/snapshots.csv merge=union
data/poll_averages.csv merge=union

# Deliberately NOT union-merged: these are regenerated in full on every run
# rather than appended to, so combining two versions would interleave two
# complete copies of the same data.
#   data/raw_polls.csv
#   data/poll_probabilities.csv
#   data/poll_history.csv
#   data/race_meta.json

